{
  "version": 195,
  "released": "2026-08-22",
  "changelog": "v195: chronology with basis — the timeline holds dates, and the fifth child interaction places them. NEW system/chronology.py: DateRecord {best, earliest, latest, granularity, confidence, basis, anchors, provenance} over three closed vocabularies, EDTF / ISO 8601-2 level 1 storage (1984~, 198X, 1998-06, 2001-21 = spring 2001, 1984/1990, 1984/.., ../1984) that round-trips every canonical form and normalizes the human ones, display_date() that quotes the person back ('around 1984 — you said you were about 5'), and the arithmetic: from_age (birthday + a stated age), from_anchor (terminus post/ante quem), intersect, widen_for_elapsed (Huttenlocher et al. 1990; a stated certain date never decays), reconcile (scores by basis, confidence and consilience and NEVER drops a claim). TIMELINE MODEL: events carry the classifier's title (noun phrase ≤ 7 words, the thing not the telling) and a date resolved only from what the author explicitly said; periods, life chapters and places carry spans; approximate_dates finally has a writer and survives as the derived display alias; derive_chrono orders the spine by dates where they exist and is byte-identical to v194 where they do not; timeline_data() gains bands (the owner's Chapter → Places → Events hierarchy), places_by_chapter/places_by_period, and anchors; align_chapters prefers date containment; corroboration windows read the record. UNKNOWNS: every gap becomes {kind, key, label, probe} with the playbook's cheapest question, plus the new era_gap kind (a dated hole between dated eras); dependency_index/leverage/keystones (capped at 2); state/timeline_deferred.json is the \"I'll find out\" memory that goes quiet without ever being counted as outstanding; arc-plan-target --timeline [--era] plans by leverage; leverage_boost (1.2) lifts keystone-adjacent questions in the weekly queue through a guarded read. WRITE PATH: timeline-place gains --date/--basis/--anchor and files the rendered date into the durable correction. NEW interactions/timeline/ + system/timeline_interaction.py: the fifth child of Conversation — stages open|place|close, ONE additive output field `placed` (a date record, {\"deferred\": true}, or null) gated on TurnShape.timeline_stage with both validation layers, five timeline_gates.* lints, ten goldens including the skeleton episode and a contradiction that keeps both accounts, and the timeline-evals seat gate. DOCTRINE: asking stays anchor-first — arc_planner.BANNED_PHRASE is unchanged and now pinned against the no_year_opener lint; the classifier's rule becomes 'do not invent; do record what was said'; the compiler's 'absolute years are deliberately NOT inferred' paragraph is rewritten. Passive users are untouched: with TurnShape.timeline_stage None the output contract is byte-identical to v194 (required test). Contract: docs/pr-specs/timeline-chronology.md. Decision: ADR 0024.",
